
Once upon a time in the lush, treacherous lands of Stranglethorn Vale, a Gnome Warlock named Gnomerlock ventured forth with his Succubus, Seducer. As they navigated the treacherous terrain, Seducer's Lash of Pain struck down enemies with ease, and her Seduction kept the bandits at bay. Yet, Gnomerlock often found himself in dire straits, as the Succubus' stealth was no match for the sudden ambushes. One fateful day, a Voidwalker named Voidy joined their quest. With Voidy's Torment, Gnomerlock could taunt and shield himself, and Consume Shadows kept him healthy. Though Seducer was a formidable companion, Voidy's resilience and defensive prowess made the duo unstoppable.

Answer: Most warlocks see Voidwalkers because they provide essential defensive and taunting abilities that complement the offensive strengths of the Succubus, making the team more versatile and resilient in the face of various challenges. [end of text]


